WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.340
The Netflix fantasy series Cursed makes a
lot of changes to the classic Arthurian legend,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.200
and raises a lot of new mysteries.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.300
Here are some of the biggest questions which
are still left unanswered by the end of the

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.480
show's first season.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.430
From the very beginning, Cursed lets us know
that Nimue is eventually doomed to sink into

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.899
a deep body of water while bleeding from multiple
arrow wounds.

00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:25.340
During the closing minutes of the first season,
we finally see how that happens: While attempting

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.390
to save a wounded Merlin alongside Morgana,
Nimue is confronted by a bow and arrow-wielding

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.160
Sister Iris.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.230
Iris ignores Nimue's pleas for mercy and fires
several arrows into her.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.300
Despite Merlin's attempt to save her, Nimue
tumbles from the bridge, disappearing into

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.780
the churning waters below, and leaving the
sword of power abandoned on the bridge.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.280
When last we see her, Nimue is sinking to
her supposed death, recalling the image that

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.080
opened the season.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.860
However, despite all signs pointing to Nimue
dying, her role in the Arthurian legend as

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.780
the mystical Lady of the Lake indicates that
she'll survive... somehow.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.450
Nimue showed herself capable of tremendous
magic throughout the course of the season.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.810
Maybe Merlin will use his magic to save her,
or perhaps Nimue will save herself through

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:08.360
her own magic.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.880
When Nimue realizes that Merlin is her biological
father, she finally understands why her mother

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.700
tasked her with bringing the sword of power
to him.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.970
Even more pieces fall into place when Merlin
shows her the circumstances that led to her

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:21.880
own conception.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.479
The two met when Nimue's mother Lenore healed
Merlin from something inside his chest that

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:27.830
was causing him pain.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.840
She promptly cut him open to extract it, and
was shocked to pull out the very sword of

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.660
power that Nimue returns to him years later.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.280
Merlin mentions that the sword was his once,
but never explains how it ended up inside

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:38.700
him.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.420
The most he offers is that it wasn't an enemy
who did it, but beyond that, we never get

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.020
any information on what the sword was doing
inside Merlin's body.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:47.520
Was he hiding it?

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.530
Was it a curse?

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:51.000
We may never know -- or at least, not by the
end of season one.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:56.000
Merlin insinuates several times that he's
actually hundreds of years old, but we never

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.480
uncover the reason behind his staggeringly
long life.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.060
Originally, Merlin was born into the Fey,
but his powers seem to exceed those of the

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.180
other Fey that we meet.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.680
When we encounter Merlin in Cursed, he's been
without his magic for some time, and we later

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.000
learn that he lost his powers when Lenore
extracted the sword of power from his body.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.380
Merlin spends most of the season endeavoring
to get his magic back through various methods,

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.040
and as he does, he winds up brushing against
death quite a few times.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:25.620
At one point, after having been stabbed multiple
times through the chest, he even asks the

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.220
rhetorical question,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.200
"Why can't I die?"

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:29.680
It's a good question.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.359
Not only should his stab wounds have been
mortal, but he was shot in the heart with

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.159
an arrow earlier in the same episode.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:39.520
We see plenty of other Fey die over the course
of Cursed, so what makes Merlin different?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.020
Probably one of the biggest twists Cursed
throws at its audience comes when we learn

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.260
the true identity of the Weeping Monk that
has been terrorizing the Fey for the entire

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:48.820
season.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:49.820
"Lancelot.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.999
A long time ago my name was Lancelot."

00:02:53.999 --> 00:02:59.099
The Weeping Monk's adopted father is Father
Carden, leader of the Red Paladins, who despise

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:00.559
the Fey and their magic.

00:03:00.559 --> 00:03:04.629
But midway through the series, Gawain the
Green Knight recognizes the Weeping Monk as

00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:05.680
a fellow Fey.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.650
By the end of the season, the Weeping Monk
has turned on his adopted father, saving the

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:10.940
young Fey boy, Squirrel.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.139
Yet the reveal that the Monk was actually
named Lancelot before he was taken by Father

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.220
Carden still comes as quite a shock.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.189
Carden tells Lancelot that he spared him from
the slaughter of his village because of his

00:03:21.189 --> 00:03:25.769
ability to sense other Fey, but considering
Carden's track record, we can't believe that

00:03:25.769 --> 00:03:26.880
that's the complete story.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.840
We're curious to learn more about the young
Lancelot before Carden took him.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.860
While Cursed is up front about the identities
of legendary characters such as Merlin and

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.280
Arthur, it enjoys doling out the more famous
names of other characters throughout the course

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.040
of the season.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.829
On several occasions, characters we've met
under one name reveal that their actual name

00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:45.829
is much more familiar.

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:47.269
"Igraine was my grandmother's name.

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:49.880
Bit of a mix-up when they first brought me
here.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.460
To friends, I'm Morgana."

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.400
"Go, Squirrel!"

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.760
"I won't leave you here."

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:55.520
"Percival!"

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.240
It begs the question of whether there are
any other well known Arthurian characters

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.860
who have already made an appearance, but under
different names.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:06.159
Since Cursed plays pretty fast and loose with
the characters' backstories, we can't rule

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.000
anyone out.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.820
After all, if the chivalrous knight Lancelot
can be introduced as one of the season's most

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.600
terrifying villains, anything is possible.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:18.320
Perhaps Sister Iris or Pym will eventually
turn out to be familiar characters from the

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:22.020
legend, or a minor character will turn out
to be much more mythologically important than

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:22.600
we'd thought.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:27.560
Something about Iris has always seemed a little
strange, starting with her first meeting with

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.230
Nimue, where Iris reveals how she can spot
demons.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.340
"I just stare at them.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.500
I stare at them until I see through their
faces to their real faces."

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.200
It's clear that Iris and Nimue are likely
not going to be friends, and sure enough,

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:45.100
Iris is soon burning down the abbey and attempting
to find the Red Paladins, determined to join

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.260
their bloody cause by killing Nimue.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:51.880
But while Iris is certainly motivated by a
strong hatred of the Fey and their magic,

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.360
there seems to be more to her than that.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.700
Several times, she seems to be internally
conflicted about the path she's set for herself,

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.260
and at one point, she punishes herself for
straying from her task by burning her own

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.260
arm over an open flame, berating herself as
though she's of two minds.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.220
Between her radical hatred, her unflinching
capacity for violence, and her strange internal

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.800
debates, we wonder if there's a lot more to
Sister Iris than meets the eye.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:19.460
When Nimue asks Merlin about the sword of
power, he admits that it was once his, and

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.640
that at one time, he might have desired it
again.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.740
However, he claims his motives have since
changed.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.020
"Let me destroy it."

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.220
"What?"

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.290
"That's my true intention, if you must know
it."

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:34.370
It turns out Merlin did want the sword back
almost immediately after Lenore extracted

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:37.540
it from his chest, since he realized the sword
was tied to his magic.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:41.080
At the time, Lenore lied and told him that
she had destroyed the sword.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:45.030
But by the time he learns that Nimue is his
daughter, he seems to have experienced a true

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.560
change of heart, and seems sincere about destroying
the sword.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.010
Yet, by the end of the season, Merlin's magic
has returned, and it seems to be tied directly

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:54.610
to his reclaiming of the sword.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:58.220
The last we see of him, he survives only by
channeling the sword's magic.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:01.580
Will he still be committed to destroying the
sword, now that he's had a taste of its power

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.140
again?

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:03.760
We'll have to wait to find out.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:08.380
Nimue may be the character who spends the
most time with the sword of power, but Merlin

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.620
has the longest history with the magical object.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:14.910
The first indication of Merlin's connection
to the sword came when he was struck by lightning

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:18.500
and branded with a sword-shaped burn mark
that ran the length of his body.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:22.850
Later, we learned that the sword was at one
time Merlin's, that it somehow wound up embedded

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:26.060
inside his body, and that his magic is somehow
linked to it.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:29.020
Yet for every small detail we do know, there's
plenty we don't.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.180
Where did the sword come from before it came
into Merlin's possession, and how did it get

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.400
so strongly linked to him?

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.150
What is the source and extent of its magical
abilities?

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.540
For an object that was at the center of most
of the conflicts in Cursed's first season,

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.620
we actually know very little about it, and
are eager to learn more.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.980
Midway through Cursed's first season, King
Uther Pendragon receives a rude awakening

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:54.060
when he learns that he is not, in fact, royal
by birth as he'd always assumed.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:58.740
It turns out that when his mother was pregnant
with her son, complications in childbirth

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.480
led to the baby being delivered stillborn.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:04.800
The king had just died several months prior,
and desperate for an heir, the queen sent

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:08.100
her midwife out to pay a local peasant to
give up her baby.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.140
The midwife returned the baby to the queen,
who raised him as her own.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:15.820
Uther learns that his biological mother was
named Sylvia, and that she died shortly after

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:18.020
giving up her child, at the age of only 19.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.920
Enraged, Uther poisons the queen with spiced
wine, which is the same method she used to

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:23.600
kill Sylvia.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.160
However, as far as we know, Sylvia was the
only member of his family ever killed as part

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:32.290
of the queen's cover-up, which means his father
may still be out there, somewhere, along with

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.920
other members of his family.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.480
Will he go seeking them, or will they eventually
track him down?

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:37.900
We'll have to wait and see.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.620
Once the truth of Uther's illegitimacy begins
to come to light, the Viking ruler Cumber

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:45.240
the Ice King arrives with a claim to the throne.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:50.270
Although Cumber claims to have Pendragon lineage,
it is never clarified exactly what his relationship

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.180
to the late king was.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:55.580
The most we learn is when the midwife gives
Cumber a blood-soaked cloth, presumably from

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:56.360
the queen's stillbirth.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:59.000
"This is the blood of my cousin?"

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.000
"It is, my lord."

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.700
Perhaps his use of the word "cousin" means
that Cumber was the king's nephew.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:08.060
However, "cousin" could also be a broader
term referring to any distant relative, in

00:08:08.061 --> 00:08:12.820
which case Cumber's bloodline could have diverged
with the Pendragons several generations earlier.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:16.560
It will be interesting to see whether the
connection between Cumber and the Pendragons

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:20.460
is explored further in future seasons, and
exactly what that connection is.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:26.160
Many times throughout Cursed, Uther seems
to refer to himself in the plural, using pronouns

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.980
like "we" and "our" to express his thoughts
and opinions.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:34.180
"Tear us down, and you will suffer as we suffer."

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:39.120
There doesn't appear to be much rhyme or reason
to when he uses plural pronouns, and when

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.370
he refers to himself as "I," begging the question
of what exactly is going on here.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.460
Maybe Uther is referring to either his kingdom
or his court when he speaks in the plural,

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.240
but that doesn't feel like what is happening.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.839
At times, it almost seems like there may be
multiple consciousnesses warring inside him.

00:08:53.839 --> 00:08:58.870
Yet no one ever seems to blink at his fluid
oscillation between singular and plural pronouns,

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:03.240
suggesting that either no one notices, or
everyone has just accepted it as a strange

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:03.680
quirk.

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:08.320
We have to wonder who Uther is referring to
whenever he says "we," and if we'll ever learn

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.420
any more about them.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.940
The mysterious, shrouded character known only
as "the Widow" appears in a handful of episodes

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:17.720
to warn characters that death may be swiftly
approaching.

00:09:18.189 --> 00:09:21.380
While it's obvious that the Widow has one
foot in the world of the living, and the other

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.900
in the world of the dead, very little is ever
communicated about her own identity.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:30.399
Some sort of shared history with Merlin is
hinted at, but no real detail is ever given.

00:09:30.399 --> 00:09:35.230
Adding another intriguing layer to the mystery
of the Widow is that she's not actually immortal.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:39.339
Morgana actually manages to kill her off screen
toward the end of season one, and subsequently

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:39.940
takes her place.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:44.560
Even Morgana herself isn't entirely sure how
it happens, but her becoming the new Widow

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:48.160
suggests that the previous Widow was also
once someone else entirely.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.999
Was she someone Merlin knew?

00:09:49.999 --> 00:09:51.529
How did she become the Widow?

00:09:51.529 --> 00:09:52.680
And who was the Widow before her?

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.080
We'll just have to hold out hope that Cursed
gets a second season, so we can find out.

